    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"exams - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\":\n    \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/exams.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [exams()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function} |\n    EdgeCase\n  description: An exam timetabling problem, as a conflict graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [exams()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function} |\n    EdgeCase\n  description: An exam timetabling problem, as a conflict graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [exams()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label .doc-label-function}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: An exam timetabling problem, as a conflict graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAn exam timetabling problem, as a conflict graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/example_networks.py#L633-L695){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nexams()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\nThe 14 courses with a final exam this term at a made-up college, joined when some student\ntakes both, so their exams can't be in the same time slot. Giving each course a slot so\nthat no edge joins two courses in the same slot is graph coloring, and the fewest slots\nthat work is the graph's chromatic number.\n\nNetwork Properties:\n\n- 14 nodes (courses, labeled by name)\n- 29 edges (pairs of courses with students in common)\n- Undirected, unweighted\n- Connected\n\nNode Attributes:\n\n- `students`: the number of students enrolled in the course\n\nEdge Attributes:\n\n- `shared`: the number of students taking both courses\n\nWhat to Look For:\n\n- **Four slots are needed.** Calculus, Physics, Chemistry and Biology all share students\n  with each other, a clique of four, so no timetable has fewer than 4 slots. It's the only\n  clique of four, and there is none of five.\n- **Four slots are enough.** The chromatic number is exactly 4: the DSATUR and\n  smallest-last strategies of `greedy_color()` find a 4-slot timetable.\n- **A greedy order that wastes a slot.** The default `\"largest_first\"` strategy, which\n  schedules the courses with the most conflicts first, needs 5 slots.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The conflict graph.\n:::\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nDraw the conflicts, with each course sized by its enrollment:\n\n::: {#9aaea999 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\nexams = ec.exams()\n\nexams.plot(size_by=\"students\", label_by=\"label\", seed=5)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2d